-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the place where jmath̃ jmath̃ₚ⁻ᵖ vanishes
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $p$ a prime which is invertible in $K$ in the weak sense that $(p : K) \ne 0$. Inside the field $K((q))$ of formal Laurent series over $K$ consider the two elements $\tilde\jmath :=$ `jqModC K`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image over $K$ of the integral power series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$-type numerator `jNum`, and $\tilde\jmath_p :=$ `jqNModC K p`, its image under the ring endomorphism `qExpand` that multiplies all Laurent exponents by $p$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^p$); let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC K p` be the intermediate field $K(\tilde\jmath, \tilde\jmath_p)$ of $K((q))/K$ generated by them. A place of $F$ over $K$ is, by the structure `Place`, a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\mathrm{image}(K)$, different from all of $F$, and a principal ideal ring; for such a place $u$, $\mathrm{ord}_u$ denotes the integer-valued order function obtained from the associated adic valuation. The assertion is: if $u$ and $u'$ are two places of $F$ over $K$ such that $\mathrm{ord}_u \tilde\jmath < 0$ and $\mathrm{ord}_u(\tilde\jmath\,\tilde\jmath_p^{-p}) > 0$, and likewise $\mathrm{ord}_{u'} \tilde\jmath < 0$ and $\mathrm{ord}_{u'}(\tilde\jmath\,\tilde\jmath_p^{-p}) > 0$, then $u = u'$.
--
--   The two conditions pick out the cusp $\infty$ on the curve with function field $K(\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_p)$, a model of $X_0(p)$: $\tilde\jmath$ has a pole there and the chart element $\tilde\jmath\,\tilde\jmath_p^{-p}$ vanishes there, while at the other pole of $\tilde\jmath$ (the cusp $0$) it is the reversed combination $\tilde\jmath_p\,\tilde\jmath^{-p}$ that vanishes; the statement is thus a uniqueness-of-cusp result complementary to [`ModularCurve.cuspChartInftyZero_place_unique`](thm.html#ModularCurve.cuspChartInftyZero_place_unique). It is used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.cuspRuleStrongFor`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.cuspRuleStrongFor) in the analysis of places of the level-$p$ modular function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_cuspChartZeroInfty_place_unique.lean

